<title>USA: California Jockey directors re-elected.</title>
<headline>California Jockey directors re-elected.</headline>
<dateline>SAN MATEO, Calif. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Jockey Club said Tuesday incumbents directors Kjell Qvale, James Harris and James Conn have been re-elected to its five-member board of directors.</p>
<p>The company's shareholders also defeated a resolution calling for a mandatory retirement at 72 years of age, 58 percent of total shares voted were cast against the measure, the company said.</p>
</text>
